        "id": "ADV-2",
        "title": "First-call initialization resets outputs computed later in the same invocation",
        "basis": "The fbInit block sets PUMP_MAINT_DUE and PUMP_RUNTIME_ACC before debounce/accumulation logic runs, but rtAccNs is reset to 0 and then accumulation may occur in the same first invocation if VFD_RUN becomes TRUE. On a fresh instance no defined power-up order exists in the spec regarding whether a first-invocation run can accumulate before initialization completes, so outputs on the very first call are ambiguous.",
